{
  "_comment": [
    "Employers whose applicant-tracking system publishes an open, keyless job",
    "board. Every slug in this file was fetched and confirmed to return real",
    "JSON with a non-zero job count (the original 37 on 2026-07-28, 64 more on",
    "2026-07-29, and 186 on 2026-07-30 from a sweep of every employer in the",
    "database — 3,021 outside the US and 5,922 inside); the job counts recorded",
    "here are that day's reading and are kept only as evidence the slug was",
    "live when it was added. They are not used by the collector.",
    "",
    "The 2026-07-30 sweep is the whole pool, so the supply is now a measured",
    "quantity: roughly 3% of US filers publish a board at this bar and under 1%",
    "of the employers we hold outside the US. Do not expect another 186 without",
    "more employers. resolve_ats_boards.py --ledger records who has been asked.",
    "",
    "Adding an employer: fetch the board endpoint by hand first. Greenhouse,",
    "Ashby and Workable answer 200 with an EMPTY list for a slug that does not",
    "exist, so a slug that was mistyped looks exactly like an employer with",
    "nothing open. The collector treats a board that drops to zero as a",
    "breakage for that reason. Lever is the exception: it answers a missing",
    "slug with {\"ok\": false}, which the collector reports as that one board",
    "failing.",
    "",
    "A board is only added with at least 10 open roles. Below that a normal",
    "quiet week empties it, and an empty board is indistinguishable from a dead",
    "slug — so a tiny board buys one more employer at the price of a recurring",
    "false breakage.",
    "",
    "Nearly every employer here is one we ALREADY hold signals for. That is the",
    "point: a board makes an existing profile richer, where an unconnected",
    "employer is only a page nobody arrives at.",
    "",
    "The exception is deliberate and countable. Seventeen entries are private",
    "companies we hold no filings for at all — Stripe, Notion, Linear, Cursor,",
    "Databricks, Scale AI and the rest — seeded by hand before the resolver",
    "existed, because their hiring is worth counting even standalone. Run",
    "resolve_ats_boards.py --verify to see the current list; it names every",
    "board whose company_key holds no signals.",
    "",
    "What is NOT acceptable is the near miss, and there were two. A board filed",
    "as 'Coinbase' keys as `coinbase` while our 8-Ks are under `coinbase",
    "global`, so one company got two profiles and neither was complete. Both",
    "that and Robinhood now carry the name our filings carry.",
    "",
    "  greenhouse       https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/{slug}/jobs",
    "  lever            https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/{slug}?mode=json",
    "  ashby            https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/{slug}",
    "  workable         https://apply.workable.com/api/v1/widget/accounts/{slug}?details=true",
    "",
    "resolve_ats_boards.py does this for employers we already hold signals for,",
    "and reports the NAME EVIDENCE behind each hit. Greenhouse and Workable",
    "publish the employer's own ACCOUNT name; Lever and Ashby publish it in the",
    "title of the board page, and jobs.ashbyhq.com/robots.txt allows that page",
    "(/meeting/, /b/ and its own /api/ are the only disallowed paths, and the",
    "posting API is a different host). So an Ashby slug belonging to somebody",
    "else is caught now rather than judged.",
    "",
    "Two rules sit on top of the match, and both were paid for:",
    "",
    "  A published name LONGER than ours may only be longer by qualifiers.",
    "  Greenhouse 'byd' publishes 'BYD North America', which is BYD's own",
    "  board; Ashby 'uniti' publishes 'Uniti AI', which is not the Uniti Group",
    "  REIT whose filings we hold. Plain containment called both a match.",
    "",
    "  A name that is ONE WORD of eight characters or fewer is not evidence by",
    "  itself: words are shared between companies and coinages are not. Ashby",
    "  'ditto' published exactly 'DITTO' and matched our DITTO exactly — ours",
    "  raised $6m for menstrual-health supplements, that board is hiring",
    "  Bluetooth and database engineers. Those go to --review, which prints our",
    "  signal beside the board's roles, and are marked reviewed one at a time.",
    "",
    "  Eight is where a 3,021-employer sweep put the line. Every wrong board it",
    "  produced — Ditto, Eve, Assured, Twenty, Weave, Symphony — is eight",
    "  characters or fewer, and Symphony is why it is not seven: ours is the",
    "  Indian air-cooler manufacturer, greenhouse:symphony is the encrypted-",
    "  messaging company. Six of twenty-six candidates were wrong that way.",
    "",
    "--verify re-checks every board in this file: still fetching, still above",
    "the bar, still publishing our name. A reading is evidence about the day it",
    "was taken and no other.",
    "",
    "Company names are the employer's own spelling: Greenhouse returns it as",
    "company_name on every posting, and the Ashby and SmartRecruiters entries",
    "were spelled from the employer's own careers site. A name is never derived",
    "from the slug ('scaleai' is not 'Scaleai').",
    "",
    "One exception, and it matters: the board's own spelling is used only when",
    "it normalises to the SAME company_key as the signals we already hold. The",
    "Recursion Pharmaceuticals board is titled 'Recursion', which keys as a",
    "different employer, so that entry keeps the name we file its filings",
    "under. Otherwise the volume panel would appear on an empty second profile."
  ],
